[3736.428217, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.428631, "o", "old = '''4. Print `INTEGRITY_OK: <id>` and exit 0 if checksums match.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.428687, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.429245, "o", "5. Print `INTEGRITY_FAIL: <id> (expected=<stored>, computed=<actual>)` and exit 1 if they differ.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.429313, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.429795, "o", "6. Print `NO_CHECKSUM: <id>` and exit 2 if the stored result has no checksum field.'''\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.42986, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.430248, "o", "new = '''4. Print `INTEGRITY_OK: <id>` and exit 0 if checksums match.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.430297, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.430649, "o", "5. Print `INTEGRITY_FAIL: <id>` and exit 1 if they differ.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.430719, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.431179, "o", "6. Print `NO_CHECKSUM: <id>` and exit 2 if the stored result has no checksum field.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.43124, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.431783, "o", "7. When `--verbose` is supplied, after the `INTEGRITY_OK` or `INTEGRITY_FAIL` line, also print:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.431844, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[3736.432013, "o", "   - `Stored checksum: <hex>`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3736.432069, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
