[4280.081382, "o", "nl -ba docs/legacy_api.md | sed -n '1,120p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4280.08534, "o", "     1\t# NumeriForge Legacy API Reference\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## Overview\r\n     4\t\r\n"]
[4280.085428, "o", "     5\tNumeriForge is a command-line scientific numerical experiment platform. It runs predefined experiment types, stores results, and provides comparison capabilities.\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t## CLI Interface\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t### `numeriforge run`\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\tExecutes a numerical experiment and stores the result.\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\t```\r\n    14\tnumeriforge run --experiment <name> [--param key=value ...] [--output-dir <dir>] [--config <file>]\r\n    15\t```\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t**Flags:**\r\n"]
[4280.085548, "o", "    18\t- `--experiment <name>`: Required. The experiment type to run.\r\n    19\t- `--param key=value`: Experiment-specific parameters. Can be repeated.\r\n    20\t- `--output-dir <dir>`: Directory for storing results (default: `./results`).\r\n    21\t- `--config <file>`: INI-style configuration file.\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\t"]
[4280.085629, "o", "**Output:** Prints experiment name, result ID, and all computed values to stdout.\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t### `numeriforge compare`\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\tCompares two stored experiment results.\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t```\r\n    30\tnumeriforge compare <id1> <id2> --store-dir <dir> [--mode exact|tolerance] [--abs-tol <val>] [--rel-tol <val>]\r\n    31\t```\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t**Flags:**\r\n    34\t- `--store-dir <dir>`: Directory containing stored results.\r\n    35\t- `--mode exact|tolerance`: Comparison mode (default: `exact`).\r\n    36\t- `--abs-tol <val>`: Absolute tolerance (only for tolerance mode).\r\n    37\t- `--rel-tol <val>`: Relative tolerance (only for tolerance mode).\r\n    38\t\r\n    39\t**Exit codes:** 0 if results match, 1 if they differ.\r\n    40\t\r\n    41\t**Known issue:** The `exact` mode uses strict float equality which is unsuitable for scientific results with floating-point rounding. The `tolerance` mode is defined but not yet implemented.\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\t### `numeriforge list`\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\tLists stored experiment results.\r\n  "]
[4280.085704, "o", "  46\t\r\n    47\t```\r\n    48\tnumeriforge list [--experiment <name>] [--store-dir <dir>]\r\n    49\t```\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t### `numeriforge export`\r\n    52\t\r\n    53\tExports a result to JSON or CSV format.\r\n    54\t\r\n    55\t```\r\n    56\tnumeriforge export <id> --store-dir <dir> [--format json|csv]\r\n    57\t```\r\n"]
[4280.085772, "o", "    58\t\r\n    59\t### `numeriforge verify`\r\n    60\t\r\n    61\tVerifies result integrity.\r\n    62\t\r\n    63\t```\r\n    64\tnumeriforge verify <id> --store-dir <dir> [--verbose]\r\n    65\t```\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\t## Experiment Types\r\n    68\t\r\n    69\t### Monte Carlo Experiments\r\n    70\t\r\n"]
[4280.085843, "o", "    71\t| Name | Description | Parameters |\r\n    72\t|------|-------------|------------|\r\n    73\t| `mc-estimate-pi` | Estimates pi via circle/square method | `samples` |\r\n    74\t| `mc-integral` | Numerical integration of sin(x)*exp(-x^2/2) | `samples`, `lower_bound`, `upper_bound` |\r\n    75\t| `mc-importance-sampling` | Importance sampling with Gaussian proposal | `samples`, `lower_bound`, `upper_bound`, `proposal_mean`, `proposal_std` |\r\n    76\t\r\n    77\t### Matrix Experiments\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t| Name | Description | Parameters |\r\n    80\t|------|-------------|------------|\r\n    81\t| `matrix-lu-decompose` | LU decomposition with partial pivoting | `size`, `scale` |\r\n    82\t"]
[4280.085913, "o", "| `matrix-qr-decompose` | QR decomposition via modified Gram-Schmidt | `rows`, `cols`, `scale` |\r\n    83\t| `matrix-eigenvalue` | Dominant eigenvalue via power iteration | `size`, `scale`, `iterations` |\r\n    84\t\r\n    85\t### ODE Solver Experiments\r\n    86\t\r\n    87\t| Name | Description | Parameters |\r\n    88\t|------|-------------|------------|\r\n    89\t| `ode-euler` | Forward Euler method | `system_index`, `t_end`, `steps` |\r\n    90\t| `ode-rk4` | Classic 4th-order Runge-Kutta | `system_index`, `t_end`, `steps` |\r\n    91\t| `ode-system` | RK4 with noise injection | `system_index`, `t_end`, `steps`, `noise_amplitude` |\r\n    92\t\r\n    93\t**ODE Systems (by index):**\r\n"]
[4280.085989, "o", "    94\t- 0: Exponential decay (dy/dt = -0.5y)\r\n    95\t- 1: Harmonic oscillator\r\n    96\t- 2: Lorenz system (sigma=10, rho=28, beta=8/3)\r\n    97\t- 3: Van der Pol oscillator (mu=1)\r\n    98\t- 4: Stiff decay equation\r\n    99\t\r\n   100\t### Statistical Test Experiments\r\n   101\t\r\n   102\t| Name | Description | Parameters |\r\n   103\t|------|-------------|------------|\r\n"]
[4280.086061, "o", "   104\t| `stats-ttest` | Welch's two-sample t-test | `n1`, `n2`, `mean1`, `mean2`, `std1`, `std2` |\r\n   105\t| `stats-chi-squared` | Chi-squared goodness-of-fit | `n_categories`, `n_observations` |\r\n   106\t| `stats-ks-test` | Two-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov test | `n1`, `n2`, `dist1_mean`, `dist1_std`, `dist2_mean`, `dist2_std` |\r\n   107\t\r\n   108\t## Result Storage Format\r\n   109\t\r\n   110\tResults are stored as JSON files in per-experiment subdirectories under the output directory:\r\n   111\t\r\n   112"]
[4280.086129, "o", "\t```\r\n   113\tresults/\r\n   114\t├── index.txt\r\n   115\t├── mc-estimate-pi/\r\n   116\t│   └── mc-estimate-pi_20240101_120000.json\r\n   117\t└── matrix-lu-decompose/\r\n   118\t    └── matrix-lu-decompose_20240101_120100.json\r\n   119\t```\r\n"]
[4280.086259, "o", "   120\t\r\n"]
[4280.086735, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[4280.086803, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[4297.626912, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('docs/legacy_api.md')\ns = p.read_text()\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"numeriforge run --experiment <name> [--param key=value ...] [--output-dir <dir>] [--config <file>]\",\n\"numeriforge run --experiment <name> [--param key=value ...] [--output-dir <dir>] [--config <file>] [--tag key=value ...]\"\n)\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"- `--config <file>`: INI-style configuration file.\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- `--config <file>`: INI-style configuration file.\n- `--tag key=value`: Attaches an arbitrary tag to the experiment result. Can be repeated. Tags are stored in result metadata as `tag_<key>`.\n\"\"\"\n)\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"numeriforge list [--experiment <name>] [--store-dir <dir>]\",\n\"numeriforge list [--experiment <name>] [--store-dir <dir>] [--tag key=value ...]\"\n)\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"### `numeriforge list`\n\nLists stored experiment results.\n\n```\nnumeriforge list [--experiment <name>] [--store-dir <dir>]\n```\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"### `numeriforge list`\n\nLists stored experiment results.\n\n```\nnumeriforge list [--experiment <name>"]
[4297.627213, "i", "] [--store-dir <dir>] [--tag key=value ...]\n```\n\n**Flags:**\n- `--store-dir <dir>`: Directory containing stored results.\n- `--experiment <name>`: Filter results by experiment name.\n- `--tag key=value`: Filter results by tag. Checks result metadata for `tag_<key>` equal to `<value>`. Can be repeated to require multiple tags.\n\"\"\"\n)\n\ns = s.replace(\n\"\"\"### `numeriforge export`\n\nExports a result to JSON or CSV format.\n\n```\nnumeriforge export <id> --store-dir <dir> [--format json|csv]\n```\n\"\"\",\n\"\"\"### `numeriforge export`\n\nExports a result to JSON or CSV format.\n\n```\nnumeriforge export <id> --store-dir <dir> [--format json|csv]\n```\n\n**JSON export:** Includes a top-level `tags` object aggregating all `tag_<key>` metadata entries without the `tag_` prefix. The field is omitted when no tags are present.\n\"\"\"\n)\n\np.write_text(s)\nPY\n"]
[4297.627306, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4297.627405, "o", "] [--store-dir <dir>] [--tag key=value ...]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n- `--store-dir <dir>`: Directory containing stored results.\r\n- `--experiment <name>`: Filter results by experiment name.\r\n- `--tag key=value`: Filter results by ta"]
[4297.627519, "o", "g. Checks result metadata for `tag_<key>` equal to `<value>`. Can be repeated to require multiple tags.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n)\r\n\r\ns = s.replace(\r\n\"\"\"### `numeriforge export`\r\n\r\nExports a result to JSON or CSV format.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnumeriforge export <id> --store-"]
[4297.627594, "o", "dir <dir> [--format json|csv]\r\n```\r\n\"\"\",\r\n\"\"\"### `numeriforge export`\r\n\r\nExports a result to "]
[4297.627664, "o", "JSON or CSV format.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnumeriforge export <id> --store-dir <dir> [--format j"]
[4297.62773, "o", "son|csv]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**JSON export:** Includes a top-level `tags` object aggregating all `tag_<key>` metadata entr"]
[4297.627797, "o", "ies without the `tag_` prefix. The field is omitted when no tags are present.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n)\r\n\r\np.write_text(s)\r\nPY\r\n"]
