[4741.233657, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/legacy_api.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K147\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. **Non-reproducible results**: All stochastic experiments use a global random number generator \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[Ked with the current time. Running the same experiment twice will produce different results. There is no `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K` parameter.\r\n"]
[4741.233782, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KThis document defines the reproducibility guarantees that NumeriForge provides. It covers \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K management for deterministic execution, result integrity via checksums, and tolerance-based comparison for scientific value matching.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K11\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KAll experiment backends that use random number generation must accept a `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K` parameter:\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K13\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- The CLI must accept a `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K <integer>` flag.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K14\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- When a \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K is provided, the experiment must produce **bit-identical** results across runs on the same platform.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K15\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- When no \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b["]
[4741.233867, "o", "K is provided, the system must generate a random \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K and include it in the result metadata under the key `\"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K\"`.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K16\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- The \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K must be recorded in the result metadata regardless of how it was obtained.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K20\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KEach experiment invocation uses its own isolated random state \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[Ked with the provided or generated \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K. Experiments do not share random state with each other or with a global source.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/reproducibility_spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K24\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KGiven the same \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseed\u001b[m\u001b[K and parameters:\r\n"]
[4741.234273, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
