[5073.826137, "o", "sed -n '261,520p' storage/storage.go\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5073.828177, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[5074.10184, "i", "sed -n '1,180p' docs/legacy_api.md\n"]
[5074.102142, "o", "sed -n '1,180p' docs/legacy_api.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5074.105235, "o", "# NumeriForge Legacy API Reference\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nNumeriForge is a command-line scientific numerical experiment platform. It runs predefined experiment types, stores results, and provides comparison capabilities.\r\n\r\n## CLI Interface\r\n"]
[5074.105332, "o", "\r\n### `numeriforge run`\r\n\r\nExecutes a numerical experiment and stores the result.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnumeriforge run --experiment <name> [--param key=value ...] [--output-dir <dir>] [--config <file>] [--tag key=value ...]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n- `--experiment <name>`: Required. The experiment type to run.\r\n- `--param key=value`: Experiment-specific parameters. Can be repeated.\r\n- `--output-dir <dir>`: Directory for storing results (default: `./results`).\r\n- `--config <file>`: INI-style configuration file.\r\n"]
[5074.105405, "o", "- `--tag key=value`: Attaches an arbitrary tag to the experiment result. Can be repeated. Tags are stored in result metadata as `tag_<key>`.\r\n\r\n**Output:** Prints experiment name, result ID, and all computed values to stdout.\r\n\r\n### `numeriforge compare`\r\n\r\nCompares two stored experiment results.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnumeriforge compare <id1> <id2> --store-dir <dir> [--mode exact|tolerance] [--abs-tol <val>] [--rel-tol <val>]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n- `--store-dir <dir>`: Directory containing stored results.\r\n- `--mode exact|tolerance`: Comparison mode (default: `exact`).\r\n"]
[5074.105451, "o", "- `--abs-tol <val>`: Absolute tolerance (only for tolerance mode).\r\n- `--rel-tol <val>`: Relative tolerance (only for tolerance mode).\r\n\r\n**Exit codes:** 0 if results match, 1 if they differ.\r\n\r\n"]
[5074.105561, "o", "**Known issue:** The `exact` mode uses strict float equality which is unsuitable for scientific results with floating-point rounding. The `tolerance` mode is defined but not yet implemented.\r\n\r\n### `numeriforge list`\r\n\r\nLists stored experiment results.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnumeriforge list [--experiment <name>] [--store-dir <dir>] [--tag key=value ...]\r\n```"]
[5074.105629, "o", "\r\n\r\n### `numeriforge export`\r\n\r\nExports a result to JSON or CSV format.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnumeriforge export <id> --store-dir <dir> [--format json|csv]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**JSON export:** Includes a top-level `tags` object aggregating all `tag_<key>` metadata entries without the `tag_` prefix. The field is omitted when no tags are present.\r\n\r\n### `numeriforge verify`\r\n\r\nVerifies result integrity.\r\n\r\n```\r\nnumeriforge verify <id> --store-dir <dir> [--verbose]\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Experiment Types\r\n\r\n### Monte Carlo Experiments\r\n\r\n| Name | Description | Parameters |\r\n|------|-------------|------------|\r\n| `mc-estimate-pi` | Estimates pi via circle/square method | `samples` |\r\n"]
[5074.105695, "o", "| `mc-integral` | Numerical integration of sin(x)*exp(-x^2/2) | `samples`, `lower_bound`, `upper_bound` |\r\n| `mc-importance-sampling` | Importance sampling with Gaussian proposal | `samples`, `lower_bound`, `upper_bound`, `proposal_mean`, `proposal_std` |\r\n\r\n### Matrix Experiments\r\n\r\n| Name | Description | Parameters |\r\n|------|-------------|------------|\r\n| `matrix-lu-decompose` | LU decomposition with partial pivoting | `size`, `scale` |\r\n| `matrix-qr-decompose` | QR decomposition via modified Gram-Schmidt | `rows`, `cols`, `scale` |\r\n| `matrix-eigenvalue` | Dominant eigenvalue via power iteration | `size`, `scale`, `iterations` |\r\n\r\n"]
[5074.105762, "o", "### ODE Solver Experiments\r\n\r\n| Name | Description | Parameters |\r\n|------|-------------|------------|\r\n| `ode-euler` | Forward Euler method | `system_index`, `t_end`, `steps` |\r\n| `ode-rk4` | Classic 4th-order Runge-Kutta | `system_index`, `t_end`, `steps` |\r\n| `ode-system` | RK4 with noise injection | `system_index`, `t_end`, `steps`, `noise_amplitude` |\r\n\r\n**ODE Systems (by index):**\r\n- 0: Exponential decay (dy/dt = -0.5y)\r\n- 1: Harmonic oscillator\r\n- 2: Lorenz system (sigma=10, rho=28, beta=8/3)\r\n- 3: Van der Pol oscillator (mu=1)\r\n- 4: Stiff decay equation\r\n\r\n### Statistical Test Experiments\r\n\r\n| Name | Description | Parameters |"]
[5074.105827, "o", "\r\n|------|-------------|------------|\r\n| `stats-ttest` | Welch's two-sample t-test | `n1`, `n2`, `mean1`, `mean2`, `std1`, `std2` |\r\n| `stats-chi-squared` | Chi-squared goodness-of-fit | `n_categories`, `n_observations` |\r\n| `stats-ks-test` | Two-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov test | `n1`, `n2`, `dist1_mean`, `dist1_std`, `dist2_mean`, `dist2_std` |\r\n\r\n## Result Storage Format\r\n\r\nResults are stored as JSON files in per-experiment subdirectories under the output directory:\r\n\r\n```\r\nresults/\r\n├── index.txt\r\n"]
[5074.105889, "o", "├── mc-estimate-pi/\r\n│   └── mc-estimate-pi_20240101_120000.json\r\n└── matrix-lu-decompose/\r\n    └── matrix-lu-decompose_20240101_120100.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nEach result JSON contains:\r\n- `id`: Unique identifier\r\n- `experiment_name`: Experiment type\r\n- `timestamp`: ISO 8601 timestamp\r\n- `parameters`: Input parameters\r\n- `values`: Computed numerical values\r\n- `labels`: Human-readable labels for values\r\n"]
[5074.105999, "o", "- `metadata`: Key-value pairs with method details\r\n\r\n**Known limitation:** Results do not include integrity checksums. There is no way to verify that stored values have not been corrupted or tampered with.\r\n\r\n## Configuration File Format\r\n\r\nINI-style configuration:\r\n\r\n```ini\r\nexperiment = mc-estimate-pi\r\noutput_dir = ./results\r\nparam.samples = 100000\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Known Issues\r\n\r\n1. **Non-reproducible results**: All stochastic experiments use a global random number generator seeded with the current time. Running the same experiment twice will produce different results. There is no `--seed` parameter.\r\n\r\n2. **Broken comparison**: The `exact` comparison mode uses strict float equality (`==`), which almost always reports mismatches for scientific computations due to floating-point rounding. The `tolerance` mode is defined in the code but not implemented.\r\n\r\n3. **No integrity verification**: Results are stored without checksums. The `verify` command is a stub.\r\n"]
[5074.106088, "o", "\r\n4. **No environment tracking**: There is no record of the runtime environment (Go version, OS, architecture, CPU features) that produced a result. This makes cross-platform reproducibility impossible to verify.\r\n"]
[5074.106535, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5074.106597, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[5081.177583, "i", "nl -ba main.go | sed -n '1,180p'\n"]
[5081.177868, "o", "nl -ba main.go | sed -n '1,180p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5081.181409, "o", "     1\tpackage main\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\timport (\r\n     4\t\t\"encoding/json\"\r\n     5\t\t\"fmt\"\r\n"]
[5081.181443, "o", "     6\t\t\"math\"\r\n     7\t\t\"os\"\r\n     8\t\t\"runtime\"\r\n     9\t\t\"strconv\"\r\n    10\t\t\"strings\"\r\n"]
[5081.181586, "o", "    11\t\t\"time\"\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\t\t\"numeriforge/compare\"\r\n    14\t\t\"numeriforge/config\"\r\n    15\t\t\"numeriforge/engine\"\r\n    16\t\t\"numeriforge/storage\"\r\n    17\t)\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\tfunc usage() {\r\n    20\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, `numeriforge - Scientific Numerical Experiment Platform\r\n    21\t\r\n    22\tUsage:\r\n    23\t  numeriforge run --experiment <name> [--param key=value ...] [--output-dir <dir>] [--config <file>] [--seed <integer>]\r\n    24\t  numeriforge compare <result_id_1> <result_id_2> --store-dir <dir> [--mode exact|tolerance] [--abs-tol <val>] [--rel-tol <val>]\r\n    25\t"]
[5081.181663, "o", "  numeriforge list [--experiment <name>] [--store-dir <dir>]\r\n    26\t  numeriforge export <result_id> --store-dir <dir> [--format json|csv]\r\n    27\t  numeriforge verify <result_id> --store-dir <dir> [--verbose]\r\n    28\t  numeriforge audit <result_id> --store-dir <dir>\r\n    29\t  numeriforge audit --all --store-dir <dir>\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\tCommands:\r\n    32\t  run       Run an experiment and store the result\r\n    33\t  compare   Compare two stored results\r\n    34\t  list      List stored experiment results\r\n    35\t  export    Export a result to a different format\r\n    36\t"]
[5081.181739, "o", "  verify    Verify result integrity\r\n    37\t  audit     Audit stored result(s) for reproducibility\r\n    38\t\r\n    39\tAvailable experiments:\r\n    40\t`)\r\n"]
[5081.1818, "o", "    41\t\tfor _, name := range engine.List() {\r\n    42\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"  %s\\n\", name)\r\n    43\t\t}\r\n    44\t}\r\n    45\t\r\n    46\tfunc main() {\r\n    47\t\tif len(os.Args) < 2 {\r\n    48\t\t\tusage()\r\n    49\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\n    50\t\t}\r\n    51\t\r\n    52\t\tcmd := os.Args[1]\r\n    53\t\r\n    54\t\tswitch cmd {\r\n    55\t\tcase \"run\":\r\n"]
[5081.18186, "o", "    56\t\t\tcmdRun(os.Args[2:])\r\n    57\t\tcase \"compare\":\r\n    58\t\t\tcmdCompare(os.Args[2:])\r\n    59\t\tcase \"list\":\r\n    60\t\t\tcmdList(os.Args[2:])\r\n    61\t\tcase \"export\":\r\n    62\t\t\tcmdExport(os.Args[2:])\r\n    63\t\tcase \"verify\":\r\n    64\t\t\t"]
[5081.18192, "o", "cmdVerify(os.Args[2:])\r\n    65\t\tcase \"audit\":\r\n    66\t\t\tcmdAudit(os.Args[2:])\r\n    67\t\tcase \"help\", \"--help\", \"-h\":\r\n    68\t\t\tusage()\r\n    69\t\tdefault:\r\n    70\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"unknown command: %s\\n\", cmd)\r\n    71\t\t\tusage()\r\n"]
[5081.181979, "o", "    72\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\n    73\t\t}\r\n    74\t}\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\t// environmentMetadata returns the environment fingerprint metadata required for\r\n    77\t// reproducible experiment traces.\r\n    78\tfunc environmentMetadata() map[string]string {\r\n"]
[5081.182042, "o", "    79\t\thostname, err := os.Hostname()\r\n    80\t\tif err != nil {\r\n    81\t\t\thostname = \"unknown\"\r\n    82\t\t}\r\n    83\t\treturn map[string]string{\r\n    84\t\t\t\"env_go_version\": runtime.Version(),\r\n    85\t\t\t\"env_os\":         runtime.GOOS,\r\n    86\t\t\t\"env_arch\":       runtime.GOARCH,\r\n    87\t\t\t\"env_hostname\":   hostname,\r\n    88\t\t}\r\n    89\t}\r\n"]
[5081.182101, "o", "    90\t\r\n    91\t// environmentFromMetadata aggregates stored environment fingerprint metadata\r\n    92\t// into an export-friendly object.\r\n    93\ttype environmentInfo struct {\r\n    94\t\tGoVersion string `json:\"go_version\"`\r\n    95\t\tOS        string `json:\"os\"`\r\n    96\t\tArch      string `json:\"arch\"`\r\n    97\t\tHostname  string `json:\"hostname\"`\r\n    98\t}\r\n"]
[5081.182164, "o", "    99\t\r\n   100\tfunc environmentFromMetadata(metadata map[string]string) environmentInfo {\r\n   101\t\treturn environmentInfo{\r\n   102\t\t\tGoVersion: metadata[\"env_go_version\"],\r\n   103\t\t\tOS:        metadata[\"env_os\"],\r\n"]
[5081.182229, "o", "   104\t\t\tArch:      metadata[\"env_arch\"],\r\n   105\t\t\tHostname:  metadata[\"env_hostname\"],\r\n   106\t\t}\r\n   107\t}\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\ttype exportPayload struct {\r\n   110\t\t*storage.StoredResult\r\n   111\t\tEnvironment environmentInfo   `json:\"environment\"`\r\n   112\t\tTags        map[string]string `json:\"tags,omitempty\"`\r\n   113\t}\r\n   114\t\r\n   115\t// tagsFromMetadata collects tag_<key> metadata entries into an export-friendly\r\n   116\t// map without the tag_ prefix. It returns nil when no tags are present.\r\n   117\tfunc tagsFromMetadata(metadata map[string]string) map[string]string {\r\n"]
[5081.182305, "o", "   118\t\tif metadata == nil {\r\n   119\t\t\treturn nil\r\n   120\t\t}\r\n   121\t\ttags := map[string]string{}\r\n   122\t\tfor k, v := range metadata {\r\n   123\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(k, \"tag_\") {\r\n   124\t\t\t\ttags[k[len(\"tag_\"):]] = v\r\n   125\t\t\t}\r\n   126\t\t}\r\n"]
[5081.182369, "o", "   127\t\tif len(tags) == 0 {\r\n   128\t\t\treturn nil\r\n   129\t\t}\r\n   130\t\treturn tags\r\n   131\t}\r\n   132\t\r\n   133\t// parseTagFlag parses a --tag key=value argument and returns the metadata key\r\n   134\t// and value. It prints an error and exits when the argument is malformed.\r\n   135\tfunc parseTagFlag(arg string) (string, string) {\r\n   136\t\tparts := strings.SplitN(arg, \"=\", 2)\r\n   137\t\tif len(parts) != 2 || parts[0] == \"\" {\r\n   138\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"error: invalid tag, expected key=value: %s\\n\", arg)\r\n"]
[5081.182439, "o", "   139\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\n   140\t\t}\r\n   141\t\treturn \"tag_\" + parts[0], parts[1]\r\n   142\t}\r\n   143\t\r\n   144\t// hasMatchingTags reports whether metadata contains all requested tag filters.\r\n   145"]
[5081.182513, "o", "\tfunc hasMatchingTags(metadata map[string]string, tags map[string]string) bool {\r\n   146\t\tfor k, v := range tags {\r\n   147\t\t\tif metadata[\"tag_\"+k] != v {\r\n   148\t\t\t\treturn false\r\n   149\t\t\t}\r\n   150\t\t}\r\n   151\t\treturn true\r\n   152\t}\r\n   153\t\r\n   154\tfunc cmdRun(args []string) {\r\n   155\t\tvar experimentName, outputDir, configPath string\r\n   156\t\tvar paramStrs []string\r\n   157\t\tvar tagStrs []string\r\n   158\t\tvar seed int64\r\n   159\t\t"]
